        Listed here are the categories and which classes they
   contain.  Each category has a superclass listed after it, except
   "Foundation" which is the base for all other classes.  Class
   structuring is a tradeoff between time and space.  For instance,
   time has been gained by not subclassing the BByytteeAArrrraayy off of
   AArrrraayy but rather copying the superclass's implementation code
   into BByytteeAArrrraayy and making it a subclass of OObbjjeecctt..  This saves
   one level of dictionary searching in _msg(), and for a these
   central classes, the redundancy may be worth it.  


       FFoouunnddaattiioonn::
          Object
             Array
             ByteArray
             IdArray

       CCoolllleeccttiioonn ((OObbjjeecctt))::
          Collection
             Set
             Sequence
             Queue
             OrderedCollection

       WWiinnddoowwiinngg ((OObbjjeecctt))::
          View
             Fixture
                ArrowFixture
                ElevatorFixture
                StretchFixture
             NullView
             MenuBar
                PullDownMenu
                   TextMenu
             StdSystemView











